# Code Commenting

Edit-time standards for comments in `.ts` / `.tsx`. Canonical detail: [STYLE.md](../docs/contributors/STYLE.md) § Comments.

**Scope:** Source and test **code** only — not `docs/**/*.md` ([documentation.mdc](./documentation.mdc)).

**Precedence:** Does not replace types or exports ([typescript.mdc](./typescript.mdc)) or UI variant rules ([ui-components.mdc](./ui-components.mdc)). Comments explain **why** and behavior — not types already in signatures.

---

## JSDoc on exports

- All **new or changed public API exports** MUST have JSDoc — symbols exposed via `package.json` `exports`, package entry barrels, CLI commands, and other surfaces other packages or consumers import.
- **Internal exports** (helpers within a package, test utilities) SHOULD have JSDoc when behavior, constraints, or invariants are not obvious from the name and types alone.

Keep JSDoc **short** — not a novel:

- Brief description; add `@param` / `@returns` / `@throws` only when they add information TypeScript does not show.
- Trivial one-liner helpers (`hasFlag`, `cn`) — one line or skip if self-explanatory.
- Obvious re-exports — no block; do not restate the name.

Update JSDoc in the **same** change when you touch a documented export.

---

## Required — inline comments

- Explain intent, constraints, or non-obvious behavior — not what the code already says.
- Use `// TODO:`, `// NOTE:`, `// FIXME:` for coordination; include ticket or context when known.

---

## Do not

- Narrate obvious code (`// increment i`, `// return result`).
- Write multi-paragraph JSDoc on trivial exported helpers.
- Add JSDoc blocks to non-exported internals unless clarifying a non-obvious invariant.
- Disable ESLint missing-documentation rules without a documented exception.
- Apply markdown doc layout rules here — use [documentation.mdc](./documentation.mdc) for `docs/**`.

---

## ESLint

Public exports should satisfy documentation lint. Fix missing docs on exports you touch; do not blanket-disable rules for new public API.

